WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.320
The A to Z of isms... Youngism.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.480
You'll definitely have heard of
ageism but what about youngism?

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.120
Are young people
discriminated against

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.360
in the same way old people often are?

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.280
It's hard to get much stats on this
and it's not a designated subject

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.920
in sociology or economics

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.160
but look closely
and you'll see it all around us.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.040
I've felt it and experienced it
on a personal level

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.960
and so have many of my friends.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:28.320
When I started my first job
I was told by a colleague

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.440
that young people don't know
what real hard work looks like.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.840
I was judged negatively
before I'd even done any work.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.720
Even when I used to go to the shop

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.960
having signs that say,
"Only two schoolchildren at a time"

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.480
felt like a slap in the face.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.880
We would never allow signs
that say that about old people.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.800
So why is it justified
when it comes to young people?

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.640
And then there's youngism
at a societal level.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.920
Young people are treated differently
because of their age.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.720
They aren't given the same political
rights and opportunities as adults.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.480
While no-one is suggesting

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.400
that babies should
be heading to the polls,

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.000
many do believe
that 16 and 17-year-olds

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:06.680
should have the right to vote

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.400
as they now do in Scotland.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.000
Young people are also treated
unfairly in the workplace.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.040
The minimum wage for young people
is lower than adults

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.080
which means young people get paid
less for doing the exact same job.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.440
Is that fair?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.160
Even in school, which is designed
to help and nurture young people

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.840
they still often aren't treated
with respect or taken seriously.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.760
Young people get no real say
over their curriculum.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.080
Schools aren't designed
to empower them,

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.360
they are given little practical
advice to prepare them for adulthood.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.520
We can't expect someone to suddenly
become an active citizen

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:41.600
when they become an adult.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.120
That process must start much earlier.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.240
Young people are our future

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.920
but need to have the power
to change their present

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.400
if we want to create a better world.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.560
Young people have always played a
significant role in shaping society.

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.760
From the Edelweiss Pirates,
who opposed Hitler in the 30s,

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.480
to the March for our Lives protest
against gun violence,

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.800
there is a history of young people
pushing to create change

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.280
and fight for the rights
of people across the world,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.360
not just in their own communities.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.800
Young people today
are growing up knowing

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.960
that climate change is going
to threaten our world.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.320
They are likely
to never buy their own home,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.720
and if they go to university
they are going to leave

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.800
with tens of thousands
of pounds of debt

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.880
without any guaranteed job.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.520
It's young people who
are going to have to solve

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.280
the biggest issues we face today

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.560
all while facing these challenges.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.080
It's no wonder
there's a huge mental health crisis.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.240
We need to treat young people
with the respect they deserve

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.280
because if we don't
everyone loses out.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.480
Thanks for watching! :)

